---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Breadcrumb from '../components/Breadcrumb.astro';
---
<Base title="Values" description="Dangerous Robot's editorial position, plainly stated." layout="reading">
  <article class="reading">
    <Breadcrumb crumbs={[
      { label: 'Home', href: '/' },
      { label: 'Research', href: '/research' },
    ]} />
    <h1>Values</h1>

    <p>
      A short manifesto, uncited. Every other page on this site is sourced;
      this page is the editorial position.
    </p>

    <h2>AI safety is unsolved</h2>
    <p>
      Frontier AI is being deployed faster than the field can verify it is
      safe. Many people, including some who build these systems, consider
      human extinction a real possibility. Like climate change, that is an
      existential risk even though no one knows exactly how it will play out.
      Vendors publish responsibility pages, but cannot characterize what their
      own models will do.
    </p>
    <p>
      Dangerous Robot treats every vendor safety claim as a claim, not a fact.
    </p>

    <h2>AI is fueling environmental destruction</h2>
    <p>
      Large AI models burn electricity, water, and embodied carbon at
      industrial scale. Firms are rushing to build fossil fuel-powered data
      centers to win an arms race. The costs are real and worth naming.
    </p>

    <h2>AI outcomes are being decided by a small group of people</h2>
    <p>
      A handful of companies, and the people who run them, decide what gets
      built, how fast it ships, and which risks are acceptable. Most of the
      people who will live with those choices have no say in them. This site
      exists to help more people have a say while they still can.
    </p>

    <h2>Staying human and connected to each other will be essential</h2>
    <p>
      AI is likely to change almost everything about how we work, learn, and
      relate to each other. We should be intentional about where it belongs in
      our lives and work, and keep human judgment where it matters.
    </p>

    <h2>Our contradictions</h2>
    <p>
      Dangerous Robot runs on AI to investigate AI. We critique tools we
      depend on and burn electricity doing it. The contradictions are real,
      and we won't dress them up.
    </p>
    <p>
      We try to be careful: small decisions go to small models, frontier
      models only when the task demands it. Our pipeline runs on Infomaniak,
      a Swiss provider using 100% renewable energy that <a href="https://news.infomaniak.com/en/infomaniak-inaugurates-a-revolutionary-data-center-that-recovers-100-of-its-energy-for-building-heating/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">recovers waste heat
      to warm buildings</a>.
    </p>

    <p class="signed"><a href="/about#who-runs-this">Brandon Faloona</a></p>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  article h2 {
    margin-top: var(--space-2xl);
  }

  article > p:first-of-type {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-lg);
  }

  .signed {
    margin-top: var(--space-xl);
  }
</style>
